{
  "id": "trans-F2",
  "animation": "trans",
  "name": "Transition: card opens, slower",
  "says": "transition",
  "layer": "transition",
  "themes": [],
  "when": "A chapter start where the voice points at a place or an object (\"and this house...\"): the new shot opens as a card, holds a beat to be read, then fills the frame (gta-pacing R6). Heavy: at most one every 30 s, twice per 5 minutes. Never the same transition twice in a row, and never on a sentence that carries a key fact.",
  "anchor": "The scene starts on the edit's hard cut `at` (where the incoming shot starts, inside the card) and lasts 25 frames: card in over frames 0-7, held 8-11, grows to full frame 12-24.",
  "duration": {
    "default": 0.833,
    "min": 0.833
  },
  "cut": 0,
  "tail": 25,
  "enter": 0.433,
  "enter_total": 0.833,
  "exit": 0,
  "exit_total": 0,
  "text": [],
  "identity": [],
  "files": [],
  "required": [],
  "vars": {},
  "window": "The scene plays assets/transitions/SCENE_ID.mp4 (25 frames): make_scene writes that path when it renames the scene, so bake that exact file with the recipe before rendering. It is not a variable: HyperFrames only extracts video frames from a src written in the file (a src bound with data-var-src renders blank), and make_scene checks file variables before it renames the scene.",
